course: dictionary
lesson: 2446
title: Damp: a little wet
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Damp means a little wet, not fully wet. Read the words around it to find its meaning. «Leave a slice of bread in a warm, damp place and in a few days fuzzy spots of mould appear.» Mould needs some wetness to grow, so damp here means a small amount of wet, not soaking.
explain: Damp can also be a noun, the wetness in the air or in the walls of a house. «A frog needs two habitats: adult frogs hunt insects on damp land, so losing ponds means losing frogs.» Land that is damp is not flooded, but it is wet enough for frogs and insects to live there.
explain: Damp can be an adjective, a verb, or a noun. As an adjective it changes: damp, damper, dampest. As a verb, dampen means to make something a little wet. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if "a little wet" still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Damp means a little wet, not fully wet.
fact: Damp can also be a noun: the wetness in the air or in the walls of a house, which can make mould grow.
fact: Damp compares as damp, damper, dampest.
fact: Seeds need damp soil to sprout, and woodlice and worms like damp places.
fact: «Dampen» means to make something a little wet.
exercise: «Leave a slice of bread in a warm, damp place and in a few days fuzzy spots of mould appear.» What does damp mean here? | Covered in paint | Very dry and hot | *A little wet | Frozen solid
exercise: «Adult frogs hunt insects on damp land.» Where do adult frogs hunt? | Inside a sealed box | *On land that is a little wet | In the sky | On hot, dry rock
exercise: Which word means to make something a little wet? | frozen | bright | cloth | *dampen
test: Which word means a little wet, not fully wet? | Soaking | Dusty | *Damp | Boiling
test: You want to compare two cloths, one more wet than the other. Which word is right? | dampest | dampened | damps | *damper
exam: Which sentence uses damp as a noun? | *Damp got into the old walls and grew mould | The day was damper than yesterday | She will damp the cloth gently | The grass was damp this morning
